# Netlify _redirects for executionpointconsulting.com
# Canonical domain: executionpointconsulting.com (non-www)
# Goal: one URL per page, everything else 301s to the clean version.

# 1. Force www -> root (non-www canonical)
https://www.executionpointconsulting.com/*   https://executionpointconsulting.com/:splat   301!

# 2. Strip .html so /services.html -> /services (one canonical clean URL)
/index.html        /            301!
/*.html            /:splat       301!

# Notes:
# - The 301! (with the bang) forces the redirect even if a matching file exists. Keep it.
# - Netlify already forces HTTPS once your domain has a cert, so no http->https rule needed here.
# - Order matters: www rule runs before the .html rules.
# - The /*.html rule passes the path without the extension via :splat.
#   Example: /about.html -> /about
